-- title:
--   Principal extended ideal has a generator from I
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ and $S$ be commutative rings with an $R$-algebra structure on $S$, and suppose $S$ is a local ring. Let $I$ be an ideal of $R$ and let $\pi \in S$. Assume that the ideal generated by the image of $I$ under the structure map $R \to S$, that is $I \cdot S = I.\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ S)$, equals the principal ideal $(\pi)$, and that $\pi$ is a non-zero-divisor of $S$ (an element of the submonoid `nonZeroDivisors S`). The conclusion is that there exists $g \in I$ such that the extended ideal $I \cdot S$ equals the principal ideal generated by the image of $g$ in $S$, and that this image of $g$ is itself a non-zero-divisor of $S$. Thus the hypothesised local generator $\pi$ can be replaced by the image of an honest element of $I$, retaining both the property of generating $I \cdot S$ and regularity.
--
--   This is a Nakayama-type descent statement: a principal extended ideal with a regular generator in a local ring already has a generator coming from the original ideal. It is used in the stalkwise verification that an ideal sheaf defines an effective Cartier divisor, where a germ-level generator must be upgraded to a section of the ideal over an affine open; it is cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_mem_ideal_and_map_eq_span_singleton_and_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_map_germ_eq_span_singleton`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.exists_mem_ideal_and_map_eq_span_singleton_and_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_map_germ_eq_span_singleton).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_exists_mem_and_map_eq_span_singleton_and_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_map_eq_span_singleton.lean

